notes=[
('transform','Filter, transform and total','Filtering keeps only values satisfying a condition. Transforming creates a new value for each retained item. Reducing combines them into a result. Keep these steps conceptually separate so you can test each rule.','Reports often need to select qualifying rows, adjust their values and calculate a total.',['First keep only scores at least 5. In the example that leaves 5, 8 and 9.','Double the retained values to obtain 10, 16 and 18. Add them to obtain 44.','For the exercise, use 3, 6 and 10. Keep 6 and 10, double both and add them to get 32.'],'Given scores 3, 6 and 10, keep values at least 5, double them and print their total. Do not change the original values.','Why start the total at zero?',['It is the identity value for addition','It makes every score zero','It sorts the collection'],0,'Adding zero changes nothing, and an empty selection then has a meaningful total of zero.','Filtering after transforming changes the meaning of the threshold. Decide which values the condition applies to.','Try an input with no qualifying scores. Explain why the total should be zero.'),
('counts','Build a frequency map','A map associates a key with a value. To count occurrences, use the word as the key and its count as the value. For a new word, start from zero, then increment once per occurrence.','Frequency maps summarize votes, tags and repeated events without searching the whole list for every item.',['Create an empty map before the loop. Recreating it inside the loop would lose earlier counts.','Read the old count using a zero default, add one, and store the new count.','Count the words code, read, code, code and display the count stored for code.'],'Build counts for code, read, code, code. Print how many times code occurs.','What count should an unseen word begin with?',['0','1','The size of the map'],0,'The first occurrence increments zero to one. Starting at one would overcount.','A missing-key lookup may not return a number. Supply the default explicitly.','Print the count for an absent word using a zero default. Discuss case-sensitive counting.'),
('errors','Handle invalid input deliberately','Input conversion can fail. Keep the operation that might fail inside try, handle the expected error, and return a documented fallback. This example accepts integer text and returns zero for invalid text.','A form or imported file should not crash an entire workflow because one value is malformed.',['Separate the conversion from the display. The helper returns a number, and the caller prints it.','In the valid example, conversion returns 12. In the invalid example, error handling returns 0.','Call the helper with "7" and "bad". Print each result on its own line.'],'Write an integer parsing helper with fallback zero. Print its results for "7" and "bad" on separate lines.','What should an error handler do?',['Use an intentional recovery rule','Hide every bug without explanation','Always stop the whole app'],0,'Recovery should follow the function contract. In real systems you may report an error instead of silently substituting a value.','A zero fallback cannot distinguish invalid text from a real zero. Use a richer result when that distinction matters.','Design an alternative result containing both a success flag and a value.'),
('objects','Bundle state and behavior in a class','A class describes objects that have related state and operations. Each instance has its own stored value. A constructor initializes that value; a method changes or reads it.','Classes can model a counter, shopping cart or game character without spreading its state across unrelated variables.',['Define the Counter class with a value and an increment method.','Create one object with an initial value. Calling its method changes that object.','For the exercise, start at 5, call increment twice, then print the resulting value.'],'Create a Counter starting at 5. Increment twice and display 7.','What happens when two separate Counter objects are created?',['Each has its own instance state','They must share the same value'],0,'Instance fields belong to their individual objects; static or class-level fields have different behavior.','Do not accidentally use shared class-level state for a value that belongs to each instance.','Create counters starting at 0 and 10. Increment only one and inspect both.'),
('recursion','Reason about recursive calls','Recursion solves a problem using a smaller version of itself. A base case stops the calls. Factorial for a nonnegative integer n is n times factorial(n−1), with factorial(0) = 1. The call stack remembers work waiting to finish.','Recursive thinking prepares you to traverse trees and break problems into smaller pieces.',['Trace factorial(4): 4 × factorial(3), then 3 × factorial(2), then 2 × factorial(1).','At 1, return 1. Unwind the pending multiplications to obtain 24.','Use the same function for 5 and 0. Print 120 and 1 on separate lines.'],'Implement recursive factorial for nonnegative integers. Print factorial(5) and factorial(0). Assume these small valid inputs.','Why must each recursive call approach a base case?',['To ensure the recursion terminates','To make every result zero'],0,'A base case helps only if recursive calls eventually reach it. Otherwise the stack keeps growing.','This small example does not validate negative input or support arbitrarily large results. Java int overflows for sufficiently large factorials.','Add negative-input validation. Compare an iterative version: both use O(n) time, but recursion uses O(n) call-stack space.'),
('binary','Shrink a search interval','Binary search requires sorted values. Compare the target with the middle value; discard the half that cannot contain it. Maintain the invariant that any possible match remains between low and high.','Searching a sorted large collection can take O(log n) comparisons instead of O(n).',['Start low at 0 and high at the last valid index. An empty array naturally has high = -1.','If the middle is not a match, move low to middle + 1 or high to middle - 1. The interval must shrink.','Print the result of finding 8 in [2,4,6,8], then of finding 3. Use -1 for a missing target.'],'Implement iterative binary search. Print 3 for target 8, then -1 for target 3 in [2,4,6,8].','What is essential for this algorithm?',['Sorted input','Every value being positive','Exactly four values'],0,'Ordering is what makes it safe to discard half the remaining positions.','Using low = middle can get stuck when middle equals low. Move past the tested position.','Test an empty collection and a target at index 0. With duplicates, this version returns a matching index, not necessarily the first.'),
('memo','Avoid repeated work with memoization','The naive Fibonacci recursion recomputes the same subproblems many times. Memoization caches a completed result under its input. The first request computes it; later requests reuse it. Define F(0)=0 and F(1)=1.','Caching overlapping subproblems can turn an impractical recursive algorithm into a useful one.',['Check the base cases before expanding recursive calls.','Look up n in the shared memo. If absent, calculate F(n−1)+F(n−2), store it, then return it.','Print F(8) and F(0), which should be 21 and 0. Reuse the same memo within each recursive computation.'],'Implement memoized Fibonacci and print F(8) and F(0).','Why pass the same memo into recursive calls?',['To share already computed results','To make every call start empty'],0,'A new empty cache for every call would defeat the purpose of memoization.','Memoization trades memory for saved work. With these base cases, time and cache space are O(n), and recursive stack depth is also O(n).','Count how many new values are cached for F(8). Compare with a bottom-up loop, and consider integer overflow for larger Java inputs.'),
('pipeline','Capstone: validate and summarize a basket','A data pipeline separates filtering, aggregation and business rules. Our contract ignores negative prices, totals the remaining prices, and subtracts a fixed discount of 5 only when that total is at least 30. It returns a value without changing the input.','Clear stages make changing one business rule less likely to break the others.',['Filter invalid negative prices first; do not subtract them from the total.','Sum the valid prices and choose the discount using the sum before any discount.','For [12,-2,8,20], valid values total 40 and the result is 35. For an empty basket it is 0.'],'Write summarize(prices) using the stated rules. Print the result for [12,-2,8,20] and for an empty collection.','When should the discount threshold be checked?',['Against the valid subtotal before discount','Against the first item only'],0,'The rule applies to the subtotal of all accepted prices, before applying the discount.','Do not mutate the original collection while filtering. Test exactly 30 as well as values just below it.','Add tests for all-invalid values and subtotal exactly 30. Explain the O(n) running time and how a one-pass implementation can reduce extra storage.')]
syntax={
'python':['A comprehension reads as expression for item in collection if condition; sum adds the resulting values.','dict.get(key, 0) returns the existing count or zero when the key is absent.','int(text) can raise ValueError. Catch that expected error rather than every possible exception.','__init__ initializes each instance. self refers to the instance receiving the method call.','A function can call itself by name. Each invocation has its own local n.','Use // for an integer midpoint. List indices must be integers.','The dictionary memo is passed to both recursive calls. Avoid a mutable default dictionary shared accidentally across independent calls.','A conditional expression chooses 5 if the condition is true, else 0.'],
'javascript':['filter keeps selected values, map transforms them, and reduce combines them. Arrow functions name each operation concisely.','Map.get reads a key; Map.set writes it. ?? uses zero only when the stored result is null or undefined.','Number(text) can produce NaN without throwing. This helper explicitly checks integer validity and throws an Error before catch handles it.','constructor initializes this.value; this refers to the receiving object when you call counter.increment().','Use return to give the smaller-call result back to the caller.','Math.floor produces an integer midpoint; === compares numeric values here.','The default parameter creates a Map for the outer call; recursive calls explicitly pass that same Map.','The ternary expression condition ? valueA : valueB selects the discount.'],
'java':['The enhanced for loop visits each int; += adds to the accumulator without rebuilding an array.','Map<String, Integer> states key/value types. HashMap stores entries; getOrDefault supplies the zero default.','Integer.parseInt throws NumberFormatException for invalid integer text. Catch that specific exception.','The nested static class can be used from static main. new creates an instance, and its constructor stores the initial value.','A static helper can call itself and return an int. All inputs here are small to avoid overflow.','Integer division gives the midpoint; low + (high - low) / 2 avoids adding two potentially large indices.','Map<Integer, Integer> stores each index and its result. Pass the same map to recursive calls.','The ternary expression selects the discount. An enhanced for loop can filter and total values in one pass.']}
for lang,items in programs.items():
 for i,(note,program) in enumerate(zip(notes,items)):
  slug,title,concept,why,walk,task,q,opts,ans,reason,pitfall,stretch=note
  ex,out,sol,target=program
  add(lang,slug,title,'Intermediate' if i<4 else 'Advanced',concept+' '+syntax[lang][i],why,ex,out,walk,task,sol,target,q,opts,ans,reason,pitfall,stretch)
  lessons[-1]['terms']=[
   [['Filter','Keep values that satisfy a condition.'],['Transform','Produce a new value from an existing one.']],
   [['Map','A collection associating keys with values.'],['Default','A fallback used when a value is absent.']],
   [['Exception','A signal that an operation could not proceed normally.'],['Handler','Code that responds to an expected error.']],
   [['Instance','An individual object created from a class.'],['Constructor','Code that initializes a new instance.']],
   [['Base case','An input answered without another recursive call.'],['Call stack','The pending function calls waiting to finish.']],
   [['Search interval','The positions where the target may still be found.'],['Invariant','A fact preserved while the search proceeds.']],
   [['Memoization','Remembering results to avoid repeated computation.'],['Overlapping subproblems','Smaller computations needed more than once.']],
   [['Pipeline','A sequence of clearly defined processing stages.'],['Edge case','An unusual or boundary input worth testing.']]
  ][i]
Path('src/data/foundations.json').write_text(json.dumps(lessons,indent=2)+'\n')
