html=[
('groups','Group form controls meaningfully','Intermediate','fieldset groups related inputs and legend names the group. Individual labels still identify each control. A radio group shares a name so only one value can be selected.','A delivery or study-preference form should explain both the group question and its possible answers.','<fieldset><legend>Study time</legend>\n<label><input type="radio" name="time" value="am">Morning</label>\n<label><input type="radio" name="time" value="pm">Evening</label></fieldset>', ['The fieldset contains the related controls. The legend is the group question.','Each radio is wrapped by a label, creating an accessible label without a separate for attribute.','Give both radios the same name and different values. Use the requested labels and values in your task.'],'Build a fieldset with legend Study mode, and labeled radio choices Online and In person. Both use name mode; values are online and campus.','<fieldset><legend>Study mode</legend>\n<label><input type="radio" name="mode" value="online">Online</label>\n<label><input type="radio" name="mode" value="campus">In person</label></fieldset>',[dict(selector='fieldset > legend',text='Study mode',label='Group named Study mode'),dict(selector='fieldset label input[type="radio"][name="mode"]',count=2,label='Two labeled choices in one group'),dict(selector='input[value="online"]',count=1,label='Online value'),dict(selector='input[value="campus"]',count=1,label='Campus value')],'Why share a radio name?',['To form a single-choice group','To make every input identical'],0,'Shared names group radios; distinct values identify the selected choice.','A legend does not replace individual labels.','Add a third choice and verify keyboard navigation in a full browser page.'),
('figures','Pair a figure with a caption','Intermediate','figure groups self-contained content with an optional figcaption. The caption gives context to everyone; alt text still communicates an image alternative. A caption and alternative need not repeat each other word for word.','A chart or photograph often needs a contextual explanation as well as a text alternative.','<figure><img src="study.jpg" alt="A notebook beside a laptop"><figcaption>A focused study session.</figcaption></figure>',['Place the self-contained image inside figure.','Give img meaningful alt text, then add a visible figcaption.','Use the image and text requested below. The local study photo is available in the preview.'],'Create a figure with study.jpg, alt A notebook beside a laptop, and caption My study space.','<figure>\n<img src="study.jpg" alt="A notebook beside a laptop">\n<figcaption>My study space</figcaption>\n</figure>',[dict(selector='figure img',attribute='src',value='study.jpg',label='Figure contains the image'),dict(selector='figure img',attribute='alt',value='A notebook beside a laptop',label='Text alternative'),dict(selector='figure figcaption',text='My study space',label='Visible caption')],'Does a caption automatically replace alt text?',['No','Yes'],0,'They have different jobs: the caption provides visible context and alt supplies an image alternative.','Avoid including important information only in an image.','Describe a chart with both a short alt and a longer explanatory caption.'),
('disclosure','Use a native disclosure','Intermediate','details and summary create an expandable disclosure without JavaScript. summary supplies its visible label. Put the expandable content after it. The open attribute makes the content initially visible.','FAQs and optional explanations can use a standard control with native keyboard behavior.','<details><summary>Why practise daily?</summary><p>Small regular sessions help reinforce ideas.</p></details>',['summary is the control a reader activates.','The paragraph is the content revealed by that control.','Add open when you want the explanation visible at first; the user can still collapse it.'],'Create open details with summary Study tip and a nonempty paragraph explaining a study habit.','<details open><summary>Study tip</summary><p>Explain a solution in your own words before moving on.</p></details>',[dict(selector='details[open] summary',text='Study tip',label='Named disclosure initially open'),dict(selector='details p',nonempty=True,label='Useful disclosed content')],'What does open do?',['Shows content initially','Opens another website'],0,'open sets the initial expanded state of the native details element.','Do not put interactive buttons inside the summary just to imitate an accordion.','Remove open and test opening the disclosure using the keyboard.'),
('metadata','Give a document its identity','Intermediate','A complete HTML document includes a doctype, an html language, a head with metadata, and a body with content. title names the browser tab; the viewport meta tag helps mobile browsers use the device width.','Language and document metadata improve interpretation, navigation and mobile presentation.','<!doctype html>\n<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Study notes</title></head><body><h1>Study notes</h1></body></html>',['lang describes the document language; it is not a visual style.','title belongs inside head. The visible h1 belongs inside body.','Set both title and h1 to Coding journal, and include the viewport declaration.'],'Write a document with html lang en, title Coding journal, h1 Coding journal and viewport content width=device-width, initial-scale=1.','<!doctype html>\n<html lang="en">\n<head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Coding journal</title></head>\n<body><h1>Coding journal</h1></body>\n</html>',[dict(selector='html',attribute='lang',value='en',label='Document language'),dict(selector='head title',text='Coding journal',label='Tab title'),dict(selector='body h1',text='Coding journal',label='Page heading'),dict(selector='meta[name="viewport"]',attribute='content',value='width=device-width, initial-scale=1',label='Mobile viewport metadata')],'Where does the tab title belong?',['head','A paragraph in body'],0,'The title element provides document metadata inside head.','The lesson preview shows body content only; inspect metadata in your source and the structural checks.','Add a concise description meta tag for the page.'),
('help','Associate help and error text','Advanced','aria-describedby references the IDs of text that explains a control. aria-invalid="true" marks a current invalid state. Keep a visible label too: a description supplements the name rather than replacing it.','A user should know both what a field asks for and how to correct a specific problem.','<label for="code">Course code</label><input id="code" aria-describedby="hint"><p id="hint">Use six characters.</p>',['Connect the label to the input with for and id.','Point aria-describedby to the helper or error element ID.','In this exercise, show a current error with aria-invalid and a specific message. A real app would update the state after validation.'],'Create label Email for id email. Add type email input with aria-invalid true and aria-describedby email-error. Add p id email-error containing Enter a valid email address.','<label for="email">Email</label>\n<input id="email" type="email" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="email-error">\n<p id="email-error">Enter a valid email address.</p>',[dict(selector='label[for="email"]',text='Email',label='Visible associated label'),dict(selector='input#email[type="email"][aria-invalid="true"]',attribute='aria-describedby',value='email-error',label='Invalid input references error'),dict(selector='p#email-error',text='Enter a valid email address.',label='Specific error message')],'Does aria-describedby replace a visible label?',['No','Yes'],0,'The label names the control; its description provides additional instructions or feedback.','Do not leave aria-invalid true after an error is fixed. This lesson represents one static error state.','Draft the valid state and explain which attributes and text should change.'),
('skip','Build a keyboard-friendly page structure','Advanced','A skip link gives keyboard users a shortcut past repeated navigation. Its href points to the main content ID. tabindex="-1" makes the target programmatically focusable without adding another stop to normal tab order.','On a long page, repeatedly tabbing through navigation is tiring. A clear main target offers a direct route.','<a href="#main">Skip to content</a><nav aria-label="Primary">Navigation</nav><main id="main" tabindex="-1"><h1>Learning</h1></main>',['Place the skip link before repeated navigation.','Match its fragment URL with the main element ID exactly.','Give navigation a useful label and the main content a heading. In this safe preview link navigation is disabled; test a downloaded page for the full focus behavior.'],'Create a Skip to content link to #content, nav aria-label Primary, and main id content tabindex -1 with an h1.','<a href="#content">Skip to content</a>\n<nav aria-label="Primary">Course navigation</nav>\n<main id="content" tabindex="-1"><h1>My learning space</h1></main>',[dict(selector='a[href="#content"]',text='Skip to content',label='Skip link destination'),dict(selector='nav',attribute='aria-label',value='Primary',label='Named navigation'),dict(selector='main#content[tabindex="-1"] h1',nonempty=True,label='Focusable target with heading')],'Why use tabindex -1 on the target?',['Allow focus without another normal tab stop','Remove all keyboard access'],0,'A negative tabindex allows programmatic focus while keeping the element outside sequential tab order.','A skip link with no matching target does not provide a useful shortcut.','Style the skip link so it becomes clearly visible when focused, without removing it from keyboard access.'),
('responsive-images','Describe responsive image choices','Advanced','srcset lists image candidates and their widths. sizes describes the expected rendered width. The browser combines those hints with device density and available space to choose a suitable candidate. src remains a fallback.','Sending a huge image to a small device wastes bandwidth; sending only a tiny image can look blurry on large screens.','<img src="study.jpg" srcset="study-small.jpg 480w, study.jpg 960w" sizes="(max-width: 600px) 100vw, 600px" alt="A study desk">',['Each w descriptor states a candidate image width, not the requested display width.','sizes expresses the planned rendered width for different viewport conditions.','Use the exact two candidates and sizes below. The preview supplies the bundled photograph for the teaching filenames.'],'Create an img with src study.jpg, srcset study-small.jpg 480w, study.jpg 960w, sizes (max-width: 600px) 100vw, 600px, and alt text A notebook beside a laptop.','<img src="study.jpg"\n srcset="study-small.jpg 480w, study.jpg 960w"\n sizes="(max-width: 600px) 100vw, 600px"\n alt="A notebook beside a laptop">',[dict(selector='img',attribute='src',value='study.jpg',label='Fallback source'),dict(selector='img',attribute='srcset',value='study-small.jpg 480w, study.jpg 960w',label='Candidate widths'),dict(selector='img',attribute='sizes',value='(max-width: 600px) 100vw, 600px',label='Planned rendered size'),dict(selector='img',attribute='alt',value='A notebook beside a laptop',label='Descriptive alternative')],'What does 480w describe?',['The candidate image width','A compulsory fixed layout width'],0,'Width descriptors identify the image candidates; CSS and layout still control the rendered element size.','Candidate widths must match the real assets in a deployed site. These teaching filenames are substituted only in the sandbox preview.','Explain why responsive image selection and responsive CSS solve different problems.'),
('capstone','Capstone: an accessible enrollment form','Advanced','Combine semantic regions, associated labels, helpful descriptions and meaningful submission controls. Browser validation can improve feedback, but it is not a security boundary and never replaces validation by a server.','A form succeeds when people understand every field and can correct mistakes without guessing.','<main><h1>Join a course</h1><form><label for="name">Name</label><input id="name" name="name" required><button type="submit">Join</button></form></main>',['Create a main region and a heading describing the form purpose.','Group related controls in a fieldset with a legend, and associate each label with its control.','Use the requested name and email fields and connect the email help paragraph through aria-describedby.'],'Build main with h1 Course enrollment; a form with fieldset/legend Your details; required name input id/name name and required email input id/name email, each with a label. Email references help id email-help. Add help text and a submit button Enroll.','<main><h1>Course enrollment</h1>\n<form><fieldset><legend>Your details</legend>\n<label for="name">Name</label><input id="name" name="name" required>\n<label for="email">Email</label><input id="email" name="email" type="email" required aria-describedby="email-help">\n<p id="email-help">We will use this address for course information.</p>\n</fieldset><button type="submit">Enroll</button></form></main>',[dict(selector='main h1',text='Course enrollment',label='Page purpose'),dict(selector='form fieldset legend',text='Your details',label='Named group'),dict(selector='label[for="name"]',nonempty=True,label='Name label'),dict(selector='input#name[name="name"][required]',count=1,label='Required name'),dict(selector='label[for="email"]',nonempty=True,label='Email label'),dict(selector='input#email[name="email"][type="email"][required]',attribute='aria-describedby',value='email-help',label='Required email with help'),dict(selector='#email-help',nonempty=True,label='Help content'),dict(selector='form button[type="submit"]',text='Enroll',label='Clear action')],'Is browser validation enough for a deployed form?',['No, the server must validate too','Yes, it cannot be bypassed'],0,'Client-side checks improve usability; requests can still be created or changed outside the browser form.','The preview blocks submission. Passing structure checks does not mean a real enrollment has been sent.','Design success and error messages for a later connected version, keeping the entered values after an error.')]
for slug,title,level,concept,why,ex,walk,task,sol,checks,q,opts,ans,reason,pitfall,stretch in html:
 add('html',slug,title,level,concept,why,ex,'',walk,task,sol,'',q,opts,ans,reason,pitfall,stretch,checks=checks,terms=[['Semantic HTML','Elements chosen for their meaning and purpose.'],['Accessible name','The name assistive technology uses to identify a control.']])
fixture='<main><article class="card"><h1>Hello, CSS!</h1><p class="intro">Small steps build confidence.</p><div class="items"><span>Learn</span><span>Try</span><span>Review</span></div><button type="button">Keep learning</button></article></main>'
css=[
('tokens','Create reusable design values','Intermediate','Custom properties store reusable CSS values. Define a property such as --accent and read it with var(--accent). A shared value lets several parts of a component change together without repeating the same literal everywhere.','A consistent palette is easier to maintain than dozens of unrelated colors.',':root { --accent: navy; }\nh1 { color: var(--accent); }',['Define the custom property on :root so descendants can inherit it.','Use var(...) where a normal property expects a value.','Set --accent to teal and use it for both the heading and button text.'],'Define --accent: teal on :root. Use it for h1 color and button color.',':root { --accent: teal; }\nh1, button { color: var(--accent); }',[('html','--accent','teal','Reusable accent'),('h1','color','rgb(0, 128, 128)','Heading uses accent'),('button','color','rgb(0, 128, 128)','Button uses accent')],'What is the benefit of a shared token?',['One intentional change updates its uses','It creates more HTML elements'],0,'A single source for the value reduces duplication and accidental inconsistency.','A custom property name begins with two hyphens. A missing value can invalidate the declaration that uses it.','Add a --space token and use it for padding and gaps.'),
('alignment','Align and distribute with Flexbox','Intermediate','Flexbox has a main axis and a cross axis. justify-content distributes along the main axis; align-items aligns along the cross axis. flex-direction determines which direction those axes take.','Understanding axes avoids guessing at properties when aligning controls.','.items { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 12px; }',['Make the parent a flex container.','In the default row direction, justify-content works horizontally and align-items vertically.','Use space-around along the main axis and center on the cross axis, with a 16px gap.'],'Make .items flex, align-items center, justify-content space-around and gap 16px.','.items { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-around; gap: 16px; }',[('.items','display','flex','Flex context'),('.items','align-items','center','Cross-axis alignment'),('.items','justify-content','space-around','Main-axis spacing'),('.items','column-gap','16px','Consistent gap')],'Which property aligns on the cross axis?',['align-items','justify-content'],0,'align-items controls cross-axis alignment; its physical direction depends on flex-direction.','Aligning items needs available space to be visually noticeable.','Change direction to column and explain how both alignment properties now act.'),
('specificity','Control overrides deliberately','Intermediate','Specificity describes how targeted a selector is. For comparable normal rules, a class selector beats an element selector. The :where(...) pseudo-class contributes zero specificity, which makes component defaults easier to override.','Low-specificity defaults reduce the temptation to add !important when customizing a component.',':where(.card) { color: gray; }\n.card { color: navy; }',['Read the default rule first: :where lets it remain easy to override.','The ordinary .card rule is more specific and wins for the same property.','Set the low-specificity default gray and override .card to teal. The heading inherits the card color.'],'Use :where(.card) for gray text, then .card for teal text. Keep the heading inheriting its color.',':where(.card) { color: gray; }\n.card { color: teal; }',[('.card','color','rgb(0, 128, 128)','Card override'),('h1','color','rgb(0, 128, 128)','Inherited heading color')],'What specificity does :where add?',['Zero','More than an ID'],0,':where allows matching without increasing selector specificity, making defaults easier to override.','Source order wins only after other cascade criteria, including specificity, are tied.','Add a direct h1 color rule and explain why it overrides the inherited value.'),
('fluid','Use fluid type with limits','Intermediate','clamp(minimum, preferred, maximum) keeps a value inside bounds. A preferred viewport-relative font size can grow with space while the minimum prevents tiny text and the maximum prevents oversized headings.','Responsive type can adapt gradually instead of jumping between many breakpoints.','h1 { font-size: clamp(24px, 4vw, 40px); }',['At a 360px viewport, 4vw is 14.4px, so the minimum 24px wins.','At 800px, 4vw is 32px, which lies inside the limits.','Apply the same rule and compare both preview widths.'],'Set h1 font-size to clamp(24px, 4vw, 40px).','h1 { font-size: clamp(24px, 4vw, 40px); }',[('h1','font-size','24px','Minimum at narrow width',360),('h1','font-size','32px','Fluid size at wide width',800)],'What does the minimum protect against?',['Text becoming too small','Any line wrapping'],0,'A minimum size sets a floor; text can still wrap naturally when space is limited.','Viewport units respond to the preview frame width here, not the full application window.','Try a relative minimum in rem and think about browser font preferences.'),
('grid-areas','Design layout with named grid areas','Advanced','Named grid areas describe a two-dimensional arrangement. Give children grid-area names, then write a template that shows the intended rows. Repeating a name stretches that area across neighboring cells.','Names make a page layout easier to read and rearrange at a breakpoint.','.card { display: grid; grid-template-areas: "title title" "intro items" "action action"; gap: 16px; }\nh1 { grid-area: title; }\n.intro { grid-area: intro; }\n.items { grid-area: items; }\nbutton { grid-area: action; }',['Turn .card into the grid container.','Name the four child areas title, intro, items and action.','Use one full-width title row, intro/items on the second row, and one full-width action row.'],'Use the example grid layout with a 16px gap and the four named areas.','.card { display: grid; grid-template-areas: "title title" "intro items" "action action"; gap: 16px; }\nh1 { grid-area: title; }\n.intro { grid-area: intro; }\n.items { grid-area: items; }\nbutton { grid-area: action; }',[('.card','display','grid','Grid context'),('.card','grid-template-areas','"title title" "intro items" "action action"','Named rows'),('h1','grid-area','title','Heading area'),('.intro','grid-area','intro','Intro area'),('.items','grid-area','items','Items area'),('button','grid-area','action','Action area')],'Why repeat title across both cells?',['To span the title across two columns','To duplicate the heading content'],0,'Repeated adjacent area names describe the space occupied by one area; they do not clone the element.','Named areas must form rectangles. A disconnected shape makes the template invalid.','At a narrow breakpoint, put all four areas into a single column.'),
('focus','Make keyboard focus visible','Advanced','Keyboard focus indicates the control that will receive the next keyboard action. :focus-visible lets you style focus when the browser decides a visible indication is useful. An outline does not occupy layout space like a border does.','A learner should never lose track of the active button while navigating without a mouse.','button:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid navy; outline-offset: 4px; }',['Apply the rule to the focused button rather than to every element.','Use a strong outline with an offset so it is separated from the button edge.','The checks focus the button in a fresh frame to inspect this state. Also navigate the preview with Tab.'],'Give button:focus-visible a 3px solid navy outline and 4px outline-offset.','button:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid navy; outline-offset: 4px; }',[('button','outline-width','3px','Visible focus width',800,'focus'),('button','outline-style','solid','Solid focus outline',800,'focus'),('button','outline-color','rgb(0, 0, 128)','Navy focus outline',800,'focus'),('button','outline-offset','4px','Separated focus indicator',800,'focus')],'Why is outline useful for focus?',['It does not change the layout dimensions','It hides the control'],0,'An outline can emphasize focus without resizing the box or moving adjacent content.','Never remove the default focus indicator without providing an equally usable replacement.','Add hover styling while keeping keyboard focus distinct and visible.'),
('motion','Respect reduced-motion preferences','Advanced','Some users prefer reduced motion. The prefers-reduced-motion media query lets you reduce nonessential animation or transition effects. Start with a deliberate default and override it for that preference.','A visual effect should not make the interface uncomfortable or harder to use.','button { transition: transform 0.2s; }\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { button { transition: none; } }',['The ordinary state allows a short transform transition.','The reduce query removes the transition for users who request less motion.','The checks inspect both emulated preference states, so both branches matter.'],'Use a 0.2s transform transition on button, and disable transitions under prefers-reduced-motion: reduce.','button { transition: transform 0.2s; }\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { button { transition: none; } }',[('button','transition-duration','0.2s','Default transition',800,None,'no-preference'),('button','transition-duration','0s','Reduced-motion transition',800,None,'reduce')],'What should reduced-motion support do?',['Reduce unnecessary movement','Hide all content'],0,'The goal is to preserve information and interaction while reducing potentially uncomfortable movement.','Do not assume everyone has the same motion preference. Test both states.','Consider a loading indicator: how could you communicate progress without continuous spinning?'),
('capstone','Capstone: a responsive course component','Advanced','Combine reusable values, bounded type, wrapping layout and an accessible focus style. Test your component as a system: a change in font size or available width can affect spacing and wrapping elsewhere.','A reusable component should stay usable as content and screen sizes change.','.card { padding: 24px; }\n.items { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; }',['Give the card border-box sizing, full available width, maximum 600px, and 24px padding.','Use navy text on white, and a heading that scales from 24px through 4vw to a 40px maximum.','Arrange items as a wrapping flex row with a 12px gap. Give button focus a visible 3px solid navy outline.'],'Build the component with the stated card, heading, items and focus rules. Test narrow and wide previews.','.card { box-sizing: border-box; width: 100%; max-width: 600px; padding: 24px; color: navy; background: white; }\nh1 { font-size: clamp(24px, 4vw, 40px); }\n.items { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; }\nbutton:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid navy; outline-offset: 4px; }',[('.card','box-sizing','border-box','Predictable sizing'),('.card','max-width','600px','Maximum width'),('.card','padding-left','24px','Inner spacing'),('.card','color','rgb(0, 0, 128)','Readable text'),('.card','background-color','rgb(255, 255, 255)','White surface'),('h1','font-size','24px','Narrow heading',360),('h1','font-size','32px','Wide heading',800),('.items','display','flex','Flex arrangement'),('.items','flex-wrap','wrap','Content may wrap'),('.items','column-gap','12px','Consistent item gap'),('button','outline-width','3px','Keyboard indicator',800,'focus')],'What should you test besides a wide screenshot?',['Narrow layout and keyboard interaction','Only the logo size'],0,'A usable component needs to work across available widths and input methods, not just look good in one image.','A passing property checklist is not a complete design or accessibility review. Read the content and interact with it too.','Replace short labels with longer ones and observe wrapping. Check focus and readability after the content change.')]
css[6]=('layers','Control priority with cascade layers','Advanced','Cascade layers group style rules into named priority levels. For normal declarations, a later layer wins over an earlier layer before selector specificity is compared. This allows low-specificity component rules to override more specific base rules deliberately.','Layers make large stylesheets easier to reason about when defaults and component styling come from different sources.','@layer base, components;\n@layer base { .card .intro { color: red; } }\n@layer components { .intro { color: teal; } }',['Declare the layer order first: base before components.','The base selector is more specific, but the later components layer has higher priority for these normal declarations.','Use the two layers and selectors shown. The intro paragraph should be teal.'],'Declare base then components. Put .card .intro color red in base, and .intro color teal in components.','@layer base, components;\n@layer base { .card .intro { color: red; } }\n@layer components { .intro { color: teal; } }',[('.intro','color','rgb(0, 128, 128)','Later normal layer wins')],'Which normal layer wins in this example?',['components','base'],0,'For normal declarations the later layer takes priority, even though the earlier layer has the more specific selector.','Unlayered normal styles outrank layered normal styles. Important declarations have different layer-order behavior, so avoid adding !important without understanding it.','Reverse the declared layer order and predict the color. Then try a normal unlayered rule.')
for slug,title,level,concept,why,ex,walk,task,sol,checks,q,opts,ans,reason,pitfall,stretch in css:
 rules=[dict(selector=x[0],property=x[1],value=x[2],label=x[3],width=x[4] if len(x)>4 else 800,action=x[5] if len(x)>5 else None,motion=x[6] if len(x)>6 else None) for x in checks]
 # Motion preference is inspected via separate style sheets in a frame; preserve the original media query for evaluation.
 add('css',slug,title,level,concept,why,ex,'',walk,task,sol,'',q,opts,ans,reason,pitfall,stretch,checks=rules,fixture=fixture,terms=[['Cascade','The rules used to resolve competing CSS declarations.'],['Responsive design','Adapting presentation to available space and user needs.']])
